{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38345174",
      "title": "\"import\" & \"export\"",
      "sourceHash": "470afe5216e1605c8aa3ed14d4e6fb58568065e63149ef612474db93f0da2566",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 3.09,
          "en": "Now I wanna start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.09,
          "end": 5.25,
          "en": "refreshing your JavaScript knowledge",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.25,
          "end": 8.64,
          "en": "by first exploring this import export syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.64,
          "end": 10.26,
          "en": "I mentioned before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.26,
          "end": 13.35,
          "en": "because in this course we're going to import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.35,
          "end": 16.47,
          "en": "and export a lot of things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.47,
          "end": 17.97,
          "en": "Because in React apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.97,
          "end": 21.6,
          "en": "like in most more advanced JavaScript projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.6,
          "end": 25.2,
          "en": "it is considered a best practice to split your code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.2,
          "end": 27,
          "en": "across multiple files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27,
          "end": 29.91,
          "en": "to keep it maintainable and manageable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.91,
          "end": 31.23,
          "en": "And that's exactly what you do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.23,
          "end": 34.2,
          "en": "with help of the import and export keywords.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.2,
          "end": 37.38,
          "en": "Now for that, let's say that in the util JS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.38,
          "end": 40.8,
          "en": "we have a certain value that should be usable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.8,
          "end": 42.27,
          "en": "in other files as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.27,
          "end": 44.31,
          "en": "For example, in the app JS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 44.31,
          "end": 47.55,
          "en": "Here we could have an API key variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 47.55,
          "end": 49.74,
          "en": "and variables in JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 49.74,
          "end": 53.13,
          "en": "are created with the special let keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 53.13,
          "end": 56.1,
          "en": "But I'll get back to variables and constants",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 56.1,
          "end": 57.9,
          "en": "and some key things you should know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 57.9,
          "end": 61.44,
          "en": "about them a little bit later in this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 61.44,
          "end": 64.14,
          "en": "And in there we could store a string created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 64.14,
          "end": 67.98,
          "en": "with single or double quotes, doesn't matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 67.98,
          "end": 71.67,
          "en": "And that string could then contain some cryptic API key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 71.67,
          "end": 73.5,
          "en": "that maybe is required",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 73.5,
          "end": 77.67,
          "en": "in order to send HTDP requests to a backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 77.67,
          "end": 79.92,
          "en": "This is just a dummy example here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 79.92,
          "end": 82.47,
          "en": "but this overall section will just show you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 82.47,
          "end": 85.23,
          "en": "some dummy examples because in the end it is just",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 85.23,
          "end": 87.873,
          "en": "about refreshing your JavaScript knowledge.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 88.71000000000001,
          "end": 91.38,
          "en": "So if that API key, that value here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 91.38,
          "end": 92.67,
          "en": "this string here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 92.67,
          "end": 95.28,
          "en": "should also be available in other files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 95.28,
          "end": 97.08,
          "en": "we need to export it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 97.08,
          "end": 100.023,
          "en": "by adding the export keyword in front of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 101.07,
          "end": 105.18,
          "en": "This makes this thing, this variable here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 105.18,
          "end": 106.08,
          "en": "in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 106.08,
          "end": 109.35,
          "en": "available outside of this file as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 109.35,
          "end": 112.89,
          "en": "We can then import it in the file where it should be used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 112.89,
          "end": 115.35,
          "en": "So in this app JS file, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 115.35,
          "end": 117.18299999999999,
          "en": "by using the import keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 118.05,
          "end": 121.53,
          "en": "And then here we need opening and closing curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 121.53,
          "end": 125.61,
          "en": "And between those braces, we then refer to the name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 125.61,
          "end": 127.2,
          "en": "of the thing that's exported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 127.2,
          "end": 130.26,
          "en": "So in this case, the name of the variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 130.26,
          "end": 132.36,
          "en": "If we would be exporting a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 132.36,
          "end": 134.49,
          "en": "it would be the name of the function instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 134.49,
          "end": 136.68,
          "en": "But here it's the name of the variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 136.68,
          "end": 139.32,
          "en": "So API key written like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 139.32,
          "end": 141.32999999999998,
          "en": "And of course the casing matters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 141.32999999999998,
          "end": 145.143,
          "en": "because JavaScript is a case sensitive language.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 146.34,
          "end": 147.173,
          "en": "And then thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 147.173,
          "end": 150.24,
          "en": "we need the from keyword to let JavaScript know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 150.24,
          "end": 152.37,
          "en": "from which file we're importing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 152.37,
          "end": 155.07,
          "en": "this thing named apiKey.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 155.07,
          "end": 159.18,
          "en": "This path to the file then goes between quotes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 159.18,
          "end": 160.62,
          "en": "single or double quotes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 160.62,
          "end": 162.57,
          "en": "Again, doesn't matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 162.57,
          "end": 165.99,
          "en": "And here we then typically have a relative path starting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 165.99,
          "end": 168.81,
          "en": "with dot slash if it's in the same folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 168.81,
          "end": 170.97,
          "en": "starting with dot dot slash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 170.97,
          "end": 173.82,
          "en": "if you want to go up one folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 173.82,
          "end": 175.59,
          "en": "but here it is in the same folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 175.59,
          "end": 177.42000000000002,
          "en": "So I will use dot slash,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 177.42000000000002,
          "end": 181.92,
          "en": "and then the name of the file with the extension added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 181.92,
          "end": 185.58,
          "en": "at least if you're using just JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 185.58,
          "end": 188.28,
          "en": "Now when working in React projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 188.28,
          "end": 191.64,
          "en": "you will actually see that the extension,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 191.64,
          "end": 193.11,
          "en": "the dot JS typically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 193.11,
          "end": 194.553,
          "en": "is omitted there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 195.39,
          "end": 197.01,
          "en": "That's the case again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 197.01,
          "end": 198.81,
          "en": "because of that build process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 198.81,
          "end": 200.4,
          "en": "that's running behind the scenes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 200.4,
          "end": 203.55,
          "en": "which will add the extension behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 203.55,
          "end": 206.04,
          "en": "If you are writing just JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 206.04,
          "end": 207.72,
          "en": "without such a build process,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 207.72,
          "end": 209.97,
          "en": "you do need to add it on your own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 209.97,
          "end": 212.46,
          "en": "But throughout this course where we do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 212.46,
          "end": 214.44,
          "en": "use React projects that come",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 214.44,
          "end": 217.77,
          "en": "with such a build process that adds the extension for us,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 217.77,
          "end": 220.71,
          "en": "we will actually not add it on our own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 220.71,
          "end": 222.87,
          "en": "But here we need to do it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 222.87,
          "end": 225.6,
          "en": "And with that, this API key variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 225.6,
          "end": 228.21,
          "en": "and the value it contains will be available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 228.21,
          "end": 229.71,
          "en": "in this app JS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 229.71,
          "end": 232.29,
          "en": "even though it's defined in another file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 232.29,
          "end": 234.06,
          "en": "And here we could then, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 234.06,
          "end": 238.023,
          "en": "console log apiKey to output it in the console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 239.49,
          "end": 241.92,
          "en": "Now, very important for these import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 241.92,
          "end": 243.99,
          "en": "and export keywords to work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 243.99,
          "end": 248.28,
          "en": "you must be using this type module import here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 248.28,
          "end": 249.84,
          "en": "That's really crucial.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 249.84,
          "end": 252.81,
          "en": "Though, you will see that for the React projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 252.81,
          "end": 256.341,
          "en": "if you explore the automatically injected script text there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 256.341,
          "end": 260.97,
          "en": "you don't find this type module attribute on them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 260.97,
          "end": 262.62,
          "en": "The reason for that simply is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 262.62,
          "end": 264.75,
          "en": "that this build process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 264.75,
          "end": 268.59,
          "en": "will actually take all your imports and exports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 268.59,
          "end": 272.55,
          "en": "and basically merge all these separate files that you have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 272.55,
          "end": 275.49,
          "en": "during development into one big file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 275.49,
          "end": 278.4,
          "en": "or a bunch of big files, which are then imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 278.4,
          "end": 283.23,
          "en": "with the old school syntax in the right order.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 283.23,
          "end": 287.43,
          "en": "This is done to also make this code execute in browsers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 287.43,
          "end": 291.54,
          "en": "that don't natively support this import export syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 291.54,
          "end": 295.5,
          "en": "and also so that the browser doesn't have to download dozens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 295.5,
          "end": 297.45,
          "en": "of small JavaScript files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 297.45,
          "end": 300.09,
          "en": "but instead just a couple of bigger files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 300.09,
          "end": 302.91,
          "en": "which typically is more efficient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 302.91,
          "end": 305.43,
          "en": "And I'm just letting you know about this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 305.43,
          "end": 306.87,
          "en": "so that you don't wonder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 306.87,
          "end": 308.82,
          "en": "why this type module is missing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 308.82,
          "end": 312.99,
          "en": "on your React projects script tax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 312.99,
          "end": 315.18,
          "en": "But if you have a vanilla JavaScript app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 315.18,
          "end": 316.89,
          "en": "without such a build process,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 316.89,
          "end": 318.78,
          "en": "you do need to add this type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 318.78,
          "end": 320.313,
          "en": "module attribute here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 321.81,
          "end": 324.24,
          "en": "And with that here in this project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 324.24,
          "end": 327.18,
          "en": "if you save that and reload the app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 327.18,
          "end": 329.22,
          "en": "and you then open this console,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 329.22,
          "end": 333.27,
          "en": "you should see your apiKey being output there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 333.27,
          "end": 336.93,
          "en": "And that's of course coming from the app JS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 336.93,
          "end": 341.013,
          "en": "where we are importing it from the util JS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 342.21,
          "end": 343.95,
          "en": "Now, that's not the only variation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 343.95,
          "end": 346.92,
          "en": "of this export import syntax, though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 346.92,
          "end": 350.46,
          "en": "This is one way of exporting and importing things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 350.46,
          "end": 353.58,
          "en": "But in this course, you'll also see another way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 353.58,
          "end": 356.94,
          "en": "Besides exporting with help of the export keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 356.94,
          "end": 359.34000000000003,
          "en": "in front of a variable or function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 359.34000000000003,
          "end": 363.75,
          "en": "you can also create a so-called default export",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 363.75,
          "end": 366.15,
          "en": "by adding the default keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 366.15,
          "end": 369.99,
          "en": "Now in that case, you must not create a variable thereafter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 369.99,
          "end": 373.44,
          "en": "like this, and you also don't assign a name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 373.44,
          "end": 376.953,
          "en": "Instead you just export the value like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 378.12,
          "end": 381.84,
          "en": "So now I'm just exporting a value without a name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 381.84,
          "end": 384.18,
          "en": "And when adding the default keyword here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 384.18,
          "end": 387.36,
          "en": "I'm saying that this here, this value here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 387.36,
          "end": 391.41,
          "en": "should be the default thing that's exported by this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 391.41,
          "end": 393.24,
          "en": "And what's very important is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 393.24,
          "end": 397.29,
          "en": "that you must only have one default export per file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 397.29,
          "end": 400.473,
          "en": "If I try to add a second one, I'm getting an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 402.06,
          "end": 404.82,
          "en": "On the other hand, with the syntax we had before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 404.82,
          "end": 409.59000000000003,
          "en": "without default, you can export as many things as you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 409.59000000000003,
          "end": 412.11,
          "en": "Exporting another variable like this wouldn't",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 412.11,
          "end": 414.3,
          "en": "have been any problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 414.3,
          "end": 416.15999999999997,
          "en": "With the default keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 416.15999999999997,
          "end": 418.17,
          "en": "you directly export a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 418.17,
          "end": 421.413,
          "en": "and you must only have one default export profile.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 422.34,
          "end": 425.04,
          "en": "So I'll also add the old code here simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 425.04,
          "end": 430.04,
          "en": "so that you see the difference like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 430.56,
          "end": 434.04,
          "en": "And then app JS, the import syntax now also changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 434.04,
          "end": 436.29,
          "en": "if you have a default export.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 436.29,
          "end": 438.24,
          "en": "Instead of importing like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 438.24,
          "end": 442.05,
          "en": "you now import without curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 442.05,
          "end": 444.33,
          "en": "Instead, you just assign any name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 444.33,
          "end": 445.74,
          "en": "of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 445.74,
          "end": 447.57,
          "en": "Since the thing that's exported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 447.57,
          "end": 449.82,
          "en": "as a default doesn't have a name here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 449.82,
          "end": 452.19,
          "en": "you can use any name you want in the file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 452.19,
          "end": 453.78,
          "en": "where you want to import it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 453.78,
          "end": 456.39,
          "en": "but you do need to assign a name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 456.39,
          "end": 458.37,
          "en": "And then you still define the path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 458.37,
          "end": 461.253,
          "en": "to the file from which you want to import like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 462.9,
          "end": 467.9,
          "en": "With that, if you save this, and again you reload this file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 469.05,
          "end": 472.8,
          "en": "you will see that this again gets locked to the console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 472.8,
          "end": 476.34000000000003,
          "en": "Now with help of such a default export",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 476.34000000000003,
          "end": 479.43,
          "en": "and the respective import syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 479.43,
          "end": 480.93,
          "en": "And this is also a common way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 480.93,
          "end": 483.69,
          "en": "of exporting something and importing something,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 483.69,
          "end": 487.74,
          "en": "which is especially useful if you only have one thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 487.74,
          "end": 491.25,
          "en": "one function, or one value in the file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 491.25,
          "end": 493.89,
          "en": "where you want to export it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 493.89,
          "end": 496.2,
          "en": "This is something you will see later in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 496.2,
          "end": 499.5,
          "en": "once we explore the concept of React components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 176,
          "start": 499.5,
          "end": 501.63,
          "en": "Because there it's quite common that we only",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 177,
          "start": 501.63,
          "end": 505.44,
          "en": "have one component, one JavaScript function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 178,
          "start": 505.44,
          "end": 507.33,
          "en": "as you will learn per file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 179,
          "start": 507.33,
          "end": 510.69,
          "en": "And therefore it's quite common to export this one component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 180,
          "start": 510.69,
          "end": 514.41,
          "en": "function as a default since there are no other things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 181,
          "start": 514.41,
          "end": 516.84,
          "en": "that would be exported in that file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 182,
          "start": 516.84,
          "end": 518.16,
          "en": "but it is totally up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 183,
          "start": 518.16,
          "end": 519.63,
          "en": "which approach you prefer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 184,
          "start": 519.63,
          "end": 521.55,
          "en": "It's just important to keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 185,
          "start": 521.55,
          "end": 523.08,
          "en": "that the import syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 186,
          "start": 523.08,
          "end": 527.1,
          "en": "also changes if you use the default export syntax here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 187,
          "start": 527.1,
          "end": 528.66,
          "en": "Now, one last thing you should know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 188,
          "start": 528.66,
          "end": 531.27,
          "en": "about the export and import syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 189,
          "start": 531.27,
          "end": 534.06,
          "en": "is that if you have named exports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 190,
          "start": 534.06,
          "end": 537.09,
          "en": "as this syntax here is called, like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 191,
          "start": 537.09,
          "end": 540.3,
          "en": "and let's say you have multiple named exports,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 192,
          "start": 540.3,
          "end": 544.95,
          "en": "for example you also have another",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 193,
          "start": 544.95,
          "end": 547.68,
          "en": "special import syntax you can use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 194,
          "start": 547.68,
          "end": 551.07,
          "en": "Of course you can import those named things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 195,
          "start": 551.07,
          "end": 554.34,
          "en": "like this, import apiKey, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 196,
          "start": 554.34,
          "end": 556.62,
          "en": "I'm just going to comment out this import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 197,
          "start": 556.62,
          "end": 558.423,
          "en": "so that we don't have a name clash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 198,
          "start": 559.29,
          "end": 561.72,
          "en": "And you could then import all the named things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 199,
          "start": 561.72,
          "end": 564,
          "en": "by separating them with a comma here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 200,
          "start": 564,
          "end": 566.37,
          "en": "That's how you would import multiple things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 201,
          "start": 566.37,
          "end": 567.69,
          "en": "from the same file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 202,
          "start": 567.69,
          "end": 570.96,
          "en": "if those things are exported as named exports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 203,
          "start": 570.96,
          "end": 573.36,
          "en": "So without the default keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 204,
          "start": 573.36,
          "end": 574.38,
          "en": "And as you see here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 205,
          "start": 574.38,
          "end": 578.34,
          "en": "you can also mix the default keyword with named exports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 206,
          "start": 578.34,
          "end": 581.88,
          "en": "You just must not have more than one default export.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 207,
          "start": 581.88,
          "end": 583.41,
          "en": "But having a default export",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 208,
          "start": 583.41,
          "end": 587.07,
          "en": "in addition to some named exports is absolutely fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 209,
          "start": 587.07,
          "end": 589.89,
          "en": "But what you could now do here is that instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 210,
          "start": 589.89,
          "end": 592.71,
          "en": "of listing all the things you want to import like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 211,
          "start": 592.71,
          "end": 595.98,
          "en": "as a comma separated list between the curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 212,
          "start": 595.98,
          "end": 597.6,
          "en": "you can also import them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 213,
          "start": 597.6,
          "end": 601.71,
          "en": "by grouping them together into a JavaScript object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 214,
          "start": 601.71,
          "end": 604.71,
          "en": "And that would be done by then using a star,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 215,
          "start": 604.71,
          "end": 606.51,
          "en": "then the ask keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 216,
          "start": 606.51,
          "end": 608.04,
          "en": "and then any name of your choice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 217,
          "start": 608.04,
          "end": 610.29,
          "en": "for example, utils or util.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 218,
          "start": 610.29,
          "end": 611.373,
          "en": "Whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 219,
          "start": 612.39,
          "end": 615,
          "en": "And then again, the path to the file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 220,
          "start": 615,
          "end": 617.973,
          "en": "from which you want to import, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 221,
          "start": 619.41,
          "end": 622.8,
          "en": "With that, all the things provided by util JS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 222,
          "start": 622.8,
          "end": 625.02,
          "en": "would be grouped into this object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 223,
          "start": 625.02,
          "end": 626.52,
          "en": "and therefore, you could use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 224,
          "start": 626.52,
          "end": 629.34,
          "en": "with the default JavaScript object notation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 225,
          "start": 629.34,
          "end": 630.48,
          "en": "using its name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 226,
          "start": 630.48,
          "end": 632.13,
          "en": "and then the dot notation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 227,
          "start": 632.13,
          "end": 634.8,
          "en": "to access the thing that was named abc",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 228,
          "start": 634.8,
          "end": 638.82,
          "en": "or the thing that was named apiKey or the default export,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 229,
          "start": 638.82,
          "end": 641.643,
          "en": "which is available under a key named default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 230,
          "start": 643.23,
          "end": 646.71,
          "en": "So that's how you could then output the apiKey.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 231,
          "start": 646.71,
          "end": 648.96,
          "en": "And therefore here, if I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 232,
          "start": 648.96,
          "end": 652.53,
          "en": "I again see that apiKey here in the console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 233,
          "start": 652.53,
          "end": 656.16,
          "en": "Now by grouping multiple exported things to gather",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 234,
          "start": 656.16,
          "end": 657.513,
          "en": "into one object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 235,
          "start": 658.92,
          "end": 660.63,
          "en": "As a last side note, this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 236,
          "start": 660.63,
          "end": 665.58,
          "en": "as keyword can also be used to assign aliases.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 237,
          "start": 665.58,
          "end": 666.6,
          "en": "So for example, here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 238,
          "start": 666.6,
          "end": 670.74,
          "en": "if I go back to this named export import thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 239,
          "start": 670.74,
          "end": 674.55,
          "en": "and I'm not happy with the name abc here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 240,
          "start": 674.55,
          "end": 677.49,
          "en": "I could assign an alias by using the as keyword word",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 241,
          "start": 677.49,
          "end": 681.247,
          "en": "after the thing that I want to rename in this file here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 242,
          "start": 681.247,
          "end": 686.19,
          "en": "and I could rename it to content or whatever I want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 243,
          "start": 686.19,
          "end": 689.28,
          "en": "And now if it would console lock content here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 244,
          "start": 689.28,
          "end": 691.71,
          "en": "I would be logging the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 245,
          "start": 691.71,
          "end": 694.92,
          "en": "that is stored in that abc variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 246,
          "start": 694.92,
          "end": 697.23,
          "en": "in the util JS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 247,
          "start": 697.23,
          "end": 699.36,
          "en": "But I'm renaming it here in the file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 248,
          "start": 699.36,
          "end": 700.59,
          "en": "where I'm importing it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 249,
          "start": 700.59,
          "end": 702.99,
          "en": "with help of that special as keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 250,
          "start": 702.99,
          "end": 705.21,
          "en": "which allows us to assign an alias",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 251,
          "start": 705.21,
          "end": 706.96,
          "en": "to the thing that's being imported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 252,
          "start": 707.97,
          "end": 709.62,
          "en": "So as you can see, there are a couple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 253,
          "start": 709.62,
          "end": 713.4,
          "en": "of things you can do with this import export concept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 254,
          "start": 713.4,
          "end": 716.07,
          "en": "In the end, it is pretty straightforward",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 255,
          "start": 716.07,
          "end": 718.17,
          "en": "but you should know about these keywords",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 256,
          "start": 718.17,
          "end": 719.25,
          "en": "and how to use them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 257,
          "start": 719.25,
          "end": 721.29,
          "en": "because we are going to use them a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 258,
          "start": 721.29,
          "end": 722.44,
          "en": "throughout this course.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}